# R8 keep rules for the app. AGP combines every file in src/main/keepRules with
# its default optimising rules and the rules each library ships in its AAR/JAR.
#
# The libraries that rely on reflection already ship their own rules, so nothing
# here keeps them by hand:
#   - Retrofit (META-INF/proguard/retrofit2.pro): service interfaces, the
#     generic return types of suspend functions, Continuation.
#   - kotlinx.serialization (META-INF/com.android.tools/r8/kotlinx-serialization-common.pro):
#     the generated serializers and Companion.serializer() that Retrofit's
#     converter looks up by type at runtime (TMDB DTOs, backup JSON,
#     navigation routes, watch provider cache).
#   - Room: the generated RepertoryDatabase_Impl, created by class name.
#   - OkHttp, Coil, Navigation, Compose: their own consumer rules.
# If a release build breaks, check those first, then add a narrow rule here
# with a comment saying why.
#
# For more details, see
#   https://d.android.com/r/tools/r8/keep-rules

# Readable stack traces from a release build: keep line numbers and hide the
# original file names. Retrace with the mapping.txt saved for that release
# (app/build/outputs/mapping/release/).
-keepattributes SourceFile,LineNumberTable
-renamesourcefileattribute SourceFile
